1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:59,268
It's so bright, I really need to hang up some curtains in here.

2
00:02:01,508 --> 00:02:14,788
Last piece of the fried chicken.

3
00:02:14,788 --> 00:02:20,228
Today's game is in the sixth block of the Shishio tournament.

4
00:02:20,228 --> 00:02:24,588
My opponent is Harunobu Nikaido.

5
00:02:24,588 --> 00:02:33,548
It's almost summer vacation.

6
00:02:33,548 --> 00:02:36,588
This'll be my first game with him since I went professional.

7
00:02:36,588 --> 00:03:00,988
In the summertime, Shogi tournaments are held outside for children on department store rooftops.

8
00:03:00,988 --> 00:03:05,788
Skilled players come from all over the country to participate in a number of these small tournaments

9
00:03:05,788 --> 00:03:08,988
before they eventually join the association.

10
00:03:08,988 --> 00:03:13,608
Harunobu and I were both regulars at these kinds of events, so we'd seen each other several

11
00:03:13,608 --> 00:03:16,168
times.

12
00:03:16,168 --> 00:03:21,348
One year when we were both in elementary school, on what seemed like the hottest day ever,

13
00:03:21,348 --> 00:03:25,668
we faced off in the semi-finals.

14
00:03:25,668 --> 00:03:31,508
The heat was almost unbearable.

15
00:03:31,508 --> 00:03:33,668
Harunobu was sweating like crazy.

16
00:03:33,668 --> 00:03:36,568
He started to look like a flushed red ogre.

17
00:03:36,568 --> 00:03:41,288
He was clearly uncomfortable.

18
00:03:41,288 --> 00:03:48,328
Just looking at him made me feel uneasy.

19
00:03:48,328 --> 00:03:51,168
During the afternoon, it kept getting hotter.

20
00:03:51,168 --> 00:03:55,888
Not so much as a cool breeze anywhere.

21
00:03:55,888 --> 00:03:57,968
Harunobu was exhausted.

22
00:03:57,968 --> 00:04:00,348
I think he was anemic or something.

23
00:04:00,348 --> 00:04:10,508
His face was so pale.

24
00:04:10,508 --> 00:04:16,008
Maybe it was arrogant of me.

25
00:04:16,008 --> 00:04:22,008
I wanted to find the quickest way to checkmate and put him out of his misery.

26
00:04:22,008 --> 00:04:30,008
I knew I had to get this poor kid into a cool, air-conditioned room as soon as possible.

27
00:04:30,008 --> 00:04:38,008
However…

28
00:04:38,008 --> 00:04:43,528
As we entered the final stage, and his imminent defeat became clear, he began to use every

29
00:04:43,528 --> 00:04:47,908
last piece he had in a desperate act of resistance.

30
00:04:47,908 --> 00:04:53,008
As the tension continued to grow, a silent scream escaped his clenched teeth.

31
00:04:53,008 --> 00:05:08,008
I don't want to lose.

32
00:05:08,008 --> 00:05:14,008
At that moment, I became ashamed of my arrogance.

33
00:05:14,008 --> 00:05:17,008
I don't want to lose.

34
00:05:17,008 --> 00:05:23,008
Drenched in sweat and reeling from the heat, he simply refused to surrender.

35
00:05:23,008 --> 00:05:25,008
I don't want to lose.

36
00:05:25,008 --> 00:05:32,008
He was here because he wanted to win, just like me.

37
00:05:32,008 --> 00:05:38,008
It became a long battle.

38
00:05:38,008 --> 00:05:40,008
My victory was obvious.

39
00:05:40,008 --> 00:05:43,008
But he continued to struggle anyway.

40
00:05:43,008 --> 00:05:49,008
One move at a time, searching for a path that didn't exist.

41
00:05:49,008 --> 00:05:55,008
However, in the end, he simply ran out of moves.

42
00:05:55,008 --> 00:06:01,008
No matter how hard he tried, there was no way his king would be able to survive.

43
00:06:01,008 --> 00:06:14,008
I lost.

44
00:06:14,008 --> 00:06:21,008
Once he admitted defeat, his eyes welled up with great, big, manga-like tears.

45
00:06:21,008 --> 00:06:30,008
Amid the crying of the cicadas in the distant department store music, all I could do was silently stare at him.

46
00:06:30,008 --> 00:06:37,008
I was looking at an opponent I would probably be facing for decades to come.

47
00:06:49,008 --> 00:06:53,008
Being a pro isn't easy.

48
00:06:53,008 --> 00:06:56,008
It's like jumping onto a train that never stops.

49
00:07:00,008 --> 00:07:04,008
The only way to ever get off is by losing.

50
00:07:11,008 --> 00:07:18,008
In this small universe, the endless cycles of winning and losing are enough to make your head spin.

51
00:07:18,008 --> 00:07:21,008
There's only one goal. To win.

52
00:07:21,008 --> 00:07:23,008
To win.

53
