127
00:13:22,168 --> 00:13:22,788
And ever.

128
00:13:24,968 --> 00:13:26,288
Master Harunobu.

129
00:13:27,208 --> 00:13:27,688
Hanaoka?

130
00:13:30,428 --> 00:13:31,688
Why aren't you on vacation?

131
00:13:32,108 --> 00:13:33,648
You're supposed to be traveling the world.

132
00:13:34,048 --> 00:13:36,788
I thought you were gonna be gone for like 80 days.

133
00:13:37,008 --> 00:13:39,268
I had your grandmother take my place instead.

134
00:13:39,648 --> 00:13:41,228
10 days off was more than enough.

135
00:13:41,568 --> 00:13:43,948
It was definitely a very satisfying vacation.

136
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:49,168
Well, to be honest, I couldn't stop worrying about you, Master Harunobu.

137
00:13:49,508 --> 00:13:52,968
All of the anxiety was beginning to give me in a regular heartbeat.

138
00:13:56,008 --> 00:13:58,748
You haven't been to the hospital lately, have you?

139
00:13:59,228 --> 00:14:01,228
We need to go see the doctor right away.

140
00:14:01,768 --> 00:14:03,568
I've already given him a call.

141
00:14:06,388 --> 00:14:08,788
You don't look well. Are you in pain?

142
00:14:09,268 --> 00:14:11,328
Maybe your kidneys are acting up again.

143
00:14:12,408 --> 00:14:13,328
I'm sorry.

144
00:14:13,328 --> 00:14:15,468
No, I'm the one who's sorry.

145
00:14:15,848 --> 00:14:19,568
I bet you haven't eaten well the entire time I've been away, have you?

146
00:14:20,388 --> 00:14:21,808
I'm sorry, Hanaoka.

147
00:14:23,008 --> 00:14:24,668
There, there. I understand.

148
00:14:25,288 --> 00:14:28,308
Subsisting on hospital food alone would only add to your stress.

149
00:14:28,668 --> 00:14:30,828
It's been this way ever since you were a child.

150
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:35,288
I know how hard this has been for you all of these years.

151
00:14:35,888 --> 00:14:38,488
But it's all right. I'm here now.

152
00:14:38,968 --> 00:14:42,348
Just take it easy and we'll get you back to feeling well again.

153
00:14:42,348 --> 00:14:45,188
What about Mr. Kiriyama?

154
00:14:45,808 --> 00:14:47,308
How did the game go?

155
00:14:48,588 --> 00:14:51,528
I lost. He was too strong.

156
00:14:52,628 --> 00:14:54,988
I didn't realize how good he'd gotten.

157
00:14:55,988 --> 00:14:56,488
But...

158
00:14:56,488 --> 00:15:00,308
I swear that I'll beat him next time.

159
00:15:01,268 --> 00:15:01,768
Right.

160
00:15:03,628 --> 00:15:05,048
Of course you will.

161
00:15:05,548 --> 00:15:07,108
I believe in you.

162
00:15:07,108 --> 00:15:22,368
After my game with Nikaido,

163
00:15:22,848 --> 00:15:25,408
I decided to go back over to Akari's house.

164
00:15:26,068 --> 00:15:26,968
Like I said I would.

165
00:15:26,968 --> 00:15:31,528
Come back after your match on Monday.

166
00:15:31,948 --> 00:15:33,448
That'll be the last day of Obon.

167
00:15:33,828 --> 00:15:35,028
And we'll make more food.

168
00:15:44,848 --> 00:15:45,688
Good evening.

169
00:15:46,328 --> 00:15:46,968
It's Rei.

170
00:15:49,308 --> 00:15:50,428
It's pretty late.

171
00:15:50,548 --> 00:15:51,748
I bet you're tired now.

172
00:15:52,148 --> 00:15:53,268
You must be hungry.

173
00:15:53,848 --> 00:15:54,288
Come in.

174
00:15:55,048 --> 00:15:56,488
Sorry it took so long.

175
00:15:56,828 --> 00:15:57,488
Look, Momo.

176
00:15:57,968 --> 00:15:58,668
Rei's here.

177
00:15:59,948 --> 00:16:01,168
I brought you some pudding.

178
00:16:05,028 --> 00:16:05,788
Go on.

179
00:16:05,968 --> 00:16:06,588
Help yourself.

180
00:16:07,168 --> 00:16:08,328
I knew you'd get here late,

181
00:16:08,428 --> 00:16:09,748
so I saved you a little of everything.

182
00:16:10,768 --> 00:16:11,928
Thank you so much.

183
00:16:12,208 --> 00:16:13,608
I know you have a small appetite,

184
00:16:13,968 --> 00:16:15,888
so I made sure to leave out just a little.

185
00:16:16,168 --> 00:16:17,128
It looks delicious.

186
00:16:17,688 --> 00:16:19,428
But I don't know if I can eat it all.

187
00:16:20,268 --> 00:16:22,468
And this is for Grandma and Mom.

188
00:16:22,468 --> 00:16:24,828
I use Momo's little miniature doll set.

189
00:16:25,288 --> 00:16:25,768
Tiny!

190
00:16:25,768 --> 00:16:27,768
We want some, we want some bites.

191
00:16:27,768 --> 00:16:28,928
Tiny, tiny bites.

192
00:16:30,448 --> 00:16:33,628
Two beers takes a lot out of me these days.

193
00:16:37,948 --> 00:16:39,428
Come on now, Grandpa.

194
00:16:39,568 --> 00:16:40,668
You can't sleep yet.

195
00:16:40,828 --> 00:16:42,928
We still have to light the ceremonial fire.

196
00:16:42,928 --> 00:16:47,828
Oh, sorry, day after nine?

197
00:16:48,008 --> 00:16:48,568
You're right.

198
00:16:49,108 --> 00:16:50,548
If we do it too late,

199
00:16:50,688 --> 00:16:53,148
your mom and grandma will have a hard time going back.

200
00:16:54,068 --> 00:16:56,208
The other day, you lit the fire in the evening.

201
00:16:57,068 --> 00:16:58,128
You're right, we did.

202
00:16:58,468 --> 00:17:00,008
But that was to welcome them home.

203
00:17:00,408 --> 00:17:01,748
We lit it around dusk.

204
00:17:02,148 --> 00:17:03,068
It's like saying,

205
00:17:03,448 --> 00:17:04,988
please hurry home, please.

206
00:17:05,168 --> 00:17:06,688
We're all here waiting for you.

207
00:17:06,688 --> 00:17:10,108
And tonight is when they return.

208
00:17:10,688 --> 00:17:12,748
We light the fire after dinner, which says,

209
00:17:13,248 --> 00:17:15,088
we want you to stay as long as possible.

210
00:17:17,008 --> 00:17:18,288
For their journey home,

211
00:17:18,568 --> 00:17:21,788
we make cucumber horses to ride so they can get here faster.

212
00:17:22,308 --> 00:17:23,968
But when they leave, it's different.

213
00:17:24,368 --> 00:17:26,448
We put out oxen made from eggplants.

214
00:17:26,448 --> 00:17:31,068
That way, they can make a slow, safe return with all our gifts.

215
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:35,448
So, now it's time for us to see them off.

216
00:17:35,448 --> 00:17:58,988
They all sat together quietly watching the fire burn.

217
00:17:59,928 --> 00:18:03,028
But a kind of sadness seemed to punctuate the mood.

218
00:18:05,448 --> 00:18:08,188
They had carefully prepared the horse and oxen

219
00:18:08,188 --> 00:18:10,368
and made a lovely feast.

220
00:18:11,088 --> 00:18:14,008
They made every effort to honor the comings and goings

221
00:18:14,008 --> 00:18:15,708
of their dearly departed relatives.

222
00:18:24,748 --> 00:18:27,868
To me, it felt like a sad funeral

223
00:18:27,868 --> 00:18:30,268
that does nothing but bring back painful memories.

224
00:18:35,448 --> 00:18:50,868
There, I guess we should go back inside now.

225
00:18:51,488 --> 00:18:53,388
Time for your bath and bedtime, Momo.

226
00:18:53,388 --> 00:19:02,508
I think I'm gonna run out to the store.

227
00:19:04,508 --> 00:19:05,308
Right now?

228
